{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794509841,"nonce":"HJnmuCinnUjWZ6kizJK79oJfWlw=","message":"The Emscripten commit is e8581cc (recommitted before pushing with a clippy fix); 803b5c4 above no longer names it.\n\nPanics are caught in an Ash side module from 03ea93b, so the first gap in this issue is closed on both wasm runtimes. What it took:\n- std rebuilt with -Z build-std=std,panic_unwind, -C panic=unwind, +exception-handling, and -C llvm-args=-wasm-use-legacy-eh=false for the exnref encoding Ash emits. Ash loads and runs the module's try_table/throw without any flag.\n- On WASI with panic=unwind, Rust's unwind crate uses libunwind and imports _Unwind_RaiseException and _Unwind_DeleteException, which Ash's runtime does not define, so Ash refused the module. hxn-hl/src/unwind.rs defines both for that build only (cfg target_os = wasi, panic = unwind), throwing with llvm.wasm.throw and tag 0 as Rust's own wasm.rs shim does for wasm32-unknown-unknown, and defines the __cpp_exception tag; a panic never leaves the module, so the tag is its own.\n- Ash's hl_throw on wasm is a wasm exception. With panic=unwind an extern \"C\" export that it passes through aborts (panic_cannot_unwind), so every HashLink primitive that can throw is now extern \"C-unwind\" (generated adapters and the hand-written fixture), and hxn-hl declares hl_throw C-unwind. Native HashLink throws by longjmp and is unaffected.\n- The fixture's panic check now runs on every runtime.\nRun: tests/counter/run.sh in all eleven local modes (wasm, gen-wasm, hl and gen-hl on Ash hybrid/jit/interp, cpp, gen-cpp, gen-cppia, emcc, gen-emcc); hl and gen-hl on stock HashLink 1.15.0 on the NUC; tests/cli and tests/examples with wasm; examples and cimport on Ash. Not run: Windows, hxcpp on Linux, the browser.\nStill open from the list: Rust threads in a side module, a future settled by a host callback, the browser host, wasm32-wasip1-threads, over-aligned handles, size.","files":null}]}